---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy model — Threadmark"
  description="How Threadmark handles your team's conversations, who can see what, and what we never do."
  ogTitle="Threadmark Privacy Model"
>
  <!-- Nav placeholder (matches the main nav height) -->
  <div class="h-16 bg-mist" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <main id="main-content" class="py-16 md:py-24 bg-mist">
    <div class="container">
      <div style="max-width: 68ch; margin-inline: auto;">

        <a
          href="/"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[14px] font-bold text-ink/45 hover:text-ink mb-10 transition-colors"
        >
          <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M19 12H5M12 5l-7 7 7 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          </svg>
          Back to Threadmark
        </a>

        <h1 class="text-ink mb-3">Privacy model</h1>
        <p class="text-[14px] text-ink/40 mb-10">Last updated October 2026</p>

        <div class="prose-section space-y-8 text-[17px] text-ink/75 leading-[1.65]">

          <section aria-labelledby="consent">
            <h2 id="consent" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">Consent before capture</h2>
            <p>
              Threadmark only reads channels you explicitly add it to. Adding Threadmark to a channel is an opt-in action by a workspace admin or channel manager. Threadmark never reads channels it hasn't been invited to, and it never reads direct messages unless every participant has consented.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="private-channels">
            <h2 id="private-channels" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">Private channels and DMs</h2>
            <p>
              For private channels and direct messages, Threadmark requires the consent of every participant before any content is published to the knowledge base. When it detects something worth capturing, it asks each participant privately via a direct message. If anyone declines, nothing is published. Threadmark never shares the original message text — only a redacted summary of the outcome.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="what-we-store">
            <h2 id="what-we-store" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">What we store</h2>
            <p>
              Threadmark stores only confirmed knowledge entries — not raw message content. A knowledge entry contains: the confirmed text of the decision, fix, or answer; the channel it came from; the name of the person who confirmed it; and the date. Message text is processed transiently to generate a draft entry and is not persisted after the entry is confirmed or rejected.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="redaction">
            <h2 id="redaction" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">Automatic redaction</h2>
            <p>
              Before Threadmark drafts a knowledge entry, it scans for and redacts patterns that look like salaries, health information, national ID numbers, phone numbers, and payment card details. This redaction happens before any human sees a draft. If an entry contains sensitive patterns that can't be cleanly redacted, Threadmark declines to draft the entry and notifies the workspace admin.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="no-training">
            <h2 id="no-training" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">No shared model training</h2>
            <p>
              Your team's messages and knowledge entries are never used to train or fine-tune models that are shared with other organisations. All AI processing uses isolated, ephemeral model calls. We do not sell, license, or share message data with third parties for any purpose.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="human-review">
            <h2 id="human-review" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">Human confirmation</h2>
            <p>
              Every knowledge entry is confirmed by a real person on your team before it becomes searchable. Threadmark flags a message as a potential entry and sends it to the relevant team member for review. That person can edit, reject, or approve the draft. Nothing enters the knowledge base without a human sign-off.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="data-retention">
            <h2 id="data-retention" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">Data retention</h2>
            <p>
              Knowledge entries are retained until explicitly deleted by a workspace admin, or until the Threadmark plan is cancelled. On cancellation, all stored entries are permanently deleted within 30 days. Business and Enterprise plans may configure custom retention policies.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4">
              Transient message data (processed but not stored) is discarded immediately after processing. Audit logs (who confirmed or replaced an entry) are retained for 12 months on the Business plan and are configurable on the Enterprise plan.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="your-rights">
            <h2 id="your-rights" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">Your rights</h2>
            <p>
              Individual users can request to see what knowledge entries include information about them, request corrections, or request deletion. Workspace admins can export or delete the full knowledge base at any time from the settings panel. For GDPR data subject access requests, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@threadmark.app">privacy@threadmark.app</a>.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section aria-labelledby="contact-us">
            <h2 id="contact-us" class="text-ink text-[22px] mb-3">Questions</h2>
            <p>
              If you have questions about this privacy model, email <a href="mailto:privacy@threadmark.app">privacy@threadmark.app</a>. We respond within two business days.
            </p>
          </section>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <footer class="bg-ink py-8 border-t border-mist/10">
    <div class="container flex items-center justify-between gap-4 flex-wrap">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5 hover:opacity-80 transition-opacity">
        <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M9 5h18a7 7 0 0 1 7 7v10a7 7 0 0 1-7 7H17l-8 6v-6a7 7 0 0 1-7-7V12a7 7 0 0 1 7-7z" fill="#FBF6F0"/>
          <path d="M7 15.5 L38 13 L38.6 20.5 L7.6 23 Z" fill="#F7C948"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="text-[14px] font-extrabold text-mist tracking-[-0.02em]">threadmark</span>
      </a>
      <p class="text-[13px] text-mist/30">&copy; 2026 Threadmark. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
